# Docker BuildKit reads `.dockerignore` and never this file (podman/buildah read
# both), so `.dockerignore` beside it is an identical copy — a copy rather than a
# symlink because not every builder follows one. `task lint:ignore-files` (part
# of `lint:check`, so CI) fails the moment the two drift.
#
# The web image builds with `web/` as its context, so the repository-root
# `.containerignore` does not apply here — this file is not a duplicate of it.
#
# `.env.local` first, and it is the one that matters: it holds the origins a
# developer points their own bundle at, and copying it into the context lets it beat
# the `--build-arg` values the build was invoked with (Vite reads `.env.local` last).
# The symptom would be an image serving a bundle wired to somebody's laptop.
.env.local
.env.*.local

node_modules/
dist/
coverage/

# Neither build reads them, and both invalidate the install layer when touched.
*.md
biome.jsonc

# The desktop shell: nothing the web bundle builds from, and its `target/` alone
# is tens of gigabytes the build would otherwise copy into its context.
src-tauri/
